1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Your club already has skills.
PeerLoop helps turn them into free peer support.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Start with a clearly labelled fictional example.
Three members. Three different needs.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Noor offers Python. Sami offers mathematics. Lina offers design.
Each member asks for a different skill.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Choose the meeting date.
Suggestions must fit the members’ shared availability.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:43,000
The generated plan connects all three requests
in one 45-minute exchange.

6
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Lina helps Sami with design. Sami helps Noor with mathematics.
Noor helps Lina with Python. Every turn is explained.

7
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Move Noor’s available time to 18:00–19:00.
Sami and Lina are still available at 16:00–17:00.

8
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:17,000
After Noor’s time is changed, only one request can be fulfilled.
PeerLoop explains the remaining requests instead of hiding them.

9
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Replacing the club with the example
requires confirmation.

10
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Switch between English and Arabic.
The Arabic interface uses a right-to-left layout.

11
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Save a portable JSON club file, or print a session plan.
Confirm the suggested sessions with your group first.

12
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:50,000
A working prototype for small clubs.
Fictional examples; no measured student outcomes.
